            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0126" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860f.51/439: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Einstein</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-23T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                                1925—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 23—1:56
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>54. I understand that the Czechoslovak loan now being negotiated with the
                    National City Company will be almost entirely utilized to meet maturing
                    short-term indebtedness, although it is needed to stabilize the currency and to
                    establish a reserve for a bank of issue.</p>
                <p>Legation is in possession of information that Czechoslovak Debt Funding
                    Commission is to conclude a Government loan in Paris today, and understanding is
                    that Dillon, Read and Company will participate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Einstein</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
